---
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<section class="section" id="maven" aria-labelledby="maven-heading">
  <div class="shell editorial-layout">
    <header class="section-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">POWERED BY MAVENJ</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading" id="maven-heading">Maven Projects. Zero Friction.</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="editorial-copy">
      <p class="body-copy">Open a Maven project or <code>pom.xml</code>. TurboJ resolves dependencies, understands reactor modules, and uses the project's Java configuration.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Use configured Maven repositories and mirrors, project Java versions and toolchains, and navigation through sources and dependencies. First-time dependency resolution may need network access.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Fast Compile keeps everyday editing responsive. When you need the complete Maven lifecycle, run Maven Build explicitly.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Run and Run All Tests work from an imported Maven workspace, even when the <code>pom.xml</code> is the active editor file.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">MavenJ is an independent Java library, embedded directly in TurboJ. Importing a project does not execute its wrappers, plugins, or annotation processors.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${site.links.source}/tree/main/mavenj`}>Explore MavenJ source and documentation</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .text-link { color: var(--tj-ui-link); display: inline-block; margin-top: 12px; }
</style>
